<title>USA: Vishay says Alfred Slaner family sells stock.</title>
<headline>Vishay says Alfred Slaner family sells stock.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vishay Intertechnology Inc said on Tuesday the family and estate of Alfred Slaner, a company co-founder, sold about 1.36 million Vishay shares to pay taxes resulting from the settlement of Slaner's estate.</p>
<p>The family and estate did not expect to sell any other shares of Vishay stock, the company said.</p>
<p>Slaner, who died in 1996, had been a co-founder of the company. Vishay Intertechnology makes electronic components.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
